{
    "background_story": "Carmen was a brilliant and pioneering surgeon who had dedicated her career to advancing the field of xenotransplantation. Her groundbreaking research focused on the development of heterografts, a type of transplant that involved using organs or tissues from a different species. Carmen's work held the promise of solving the chronic shortage of human organs available for transplantation. She spent years perfecting the technique, and her team finally achieved a major breakthrough when they successfully transplanted a pig heart into a human patient. The recipient, a young woman named Sarah, made a full recovery, thanks to Carmen's innovative work. Carmen's achievement sparked a new era in transplantation medicine, and she became a leading figure in the field, hailed for her vision and expertise.",
